1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,630
Slide 14 is our first "INTERACTIVE STUDENT POLL: How many hours do you spend waiting for repetitive digital tasks each week?"

2
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:16,697
We surveyed our engineering cohort across four categories: Option A: Less than 2 hours.

3
00:00:16,697 --> 00:00:18,591
Option B: 2 to 5 hours.

4
00:00:18,591 --> 00:00:20,568
Option C: 5 to 10 hours.

5
00:00:20,568 --> 00:00:24,030
And Option D: More than 10 hours per week.

6
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:28,668
Take a moment to reflect on your own weekly routine.

7
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:39,380
Think about all the time spent manually triaging emails, reformatting spreadsheets, compiling status updates, and waiting for slow synchronous tools.

8
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:44,810
When I was an undergraduate, I tracked my time with a stopwatch for two weeks.

9
00:00:44,810 --> 00:00:54,800
I discovered that I spent over 12 hours every week just formatting CSV exports, converting PDF readings into study notes, and chasing team members for meeting availability.

10
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,031
That is an immense cognitive drain!

11
00:00:58,031 --> 00:01:04,560
Let us advance to Slide 15 to examine the surprising empirical data from our broader student body!

